Syntax:
NOT, !

Logical NOT. Evaluates to 1 if the operand is 0, to 0 if the operand is
non-zero, and NOT NULL returns NULL.

URL: http://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/5.0/en/logical-operators.html

mysql> SELECT NOT 10;
        -> 0
mysql> SELECT NOT 0;
        -> 1
mysql> SELECT NOT NULL;
        -> NULL
mysql> SELECT ! (1+1);
        -> 0
mysql> SELECT ! 1+1;
        -> 1
