Syntax:
AND, &&

Logical AND. Evaluates to 1 if all operands are non-zero and not NULL,
to 0 if one or more operands are 0, otherwise NULL is returned.

URL: http://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/5.0/en/logical-operators.html

mysql> SELECT 1 && 1;
        -> 1
mysql> SELECT 1 && 0;
        -> 0
mysql> SELECT 1 && NULL;
        -> NULL
mysql> SELECT 0 && NULL;
        -> 0
mysql> SELECT NULL && 0;
        -> 0
